## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:**create_note_for_chapter**
```plaintext
CLASS Note
    PROPERTY chapter: string
    PROPERTY content: string
    FUNCTION INIT(chapter: string, content: string)
        ASSIGN chapter TO self.chapter
        ASSIGN content TO self.content
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

CLASS NoteManager
    PROPERTY notes: list of Note
    FUNCTION INIT()
        SET self.notes TO empty list
        CALL load_notes()
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION add_note(chapter: string, content: string)
        CREATE new_note from Note with chapter, content
        APPEND new_note to self.notes
        CALL save_notes()
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION load_notes()
        TRY TO open 'notes.txt' for reading
            FOR EACH line in file
                SPLIT line by '|'
                CREATE Note with chapter, content
                APPEND the new Note to self.notes
            END FOR
        CATCH FileNotFoundError
            DO NOTHING
        END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION save_notes()
        OPEN 'notes.txt' for writing
        FOR EACH note in self.notes
            WRITE formatted note.chapter, note.content to file
        END FOR
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS
```
|Case|:**add_text_note**
```plaintext
FUNCTION save_note(book_id, chapter, note)
    OPEN self.notes_file in append mode
        WRITE (book_id + "|" + chapter + "|" + note)
    CLOSE file
```
|Case|:**organize_notes**
```plaintext
CLASS DataManager
    FUNCTION load_notes()
        IF self.notes_file does not exist THEN
            RETURN []
        ENDIF
        OPEN self.notes_file in read mode
            RETURN LIST of lines after stripping whitespace from each line
        CLOSE file
```


